Which of the following pathophysiologic processes most likely caused these findings? 
1) Coronary artery spasm; 
2) Disruption of an atherosclerotic plaque with subsequent thrombosis; 
3) Hemorrhage into an atherosclerotic plaque; 
4) Vasculitis of the coronary arteries

The correct answer is 2) Disruption of an atherosclerotic plaque with subsequent thrombosis.
